        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Nimavar school, Isfahan, Iran, Nimavar Bazaar\n- Concepts: bazaar, Persian etymology\n- Historical periods: Safavid era\n\nFacts:\n- Nimavar school is a historical school in Isfahan, Iran.\n- Nimavar school is located in Nimavar Bazaar.\n- Nimavar school belongs to the Safavid era.\n- The term bazaar originates from the Persian word bāzār.\n- The Persian word bāzār derives from Middle Persian wāzār, from Old Persian vāčar, and from Proto-Indo-Iranian *wahā-čarana.",
